The reason CodeBrain output is different is already in its script:

```python
# Codebrain/Downstream/finetune_main.py
params.model_dir = params.model_dir + params.downstream_dataset + '/'
params.log_dir = params.log_dir + params.downstream_dataset + '/'
params.output_dir = params.output_dir + params.downstream_dataset + '/' if params.output_dir else ''
```

So with:

```bash
--downstream_dataset TUAB
--output_dir ./debug_output/CodeBrain/
```

CodeBrain writes to:

```text
./debug_output/CodeBrain/TUAB/log.txt
```

CBraMod and CSBrain do **not** append `TUAB` to `output_dir`, so they write directly to:

```text
./debug_output/CBraMod/log.txt
./debug_output/CSBrain/log.txt
```

The only code patch I made was outside the repo, in the temporary connector:

```text
/nicoletye/workspace/eegfm_debug_pkl_connector/models/model_for_tuab.py
```

That was to fix the CodeBrain shape error without editing the GitHub repo.

So the output is not unified because CodeBrain’s own `finetune_main.py` adds the dataset subfolder. To make all three exactly unified, we would need either a small CodeBrain-only patch in the debug repo, or a post-run collector/normalizer script.